{"name":"Deep Diving","hex":"#5e97a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep diving","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Underwater diving to a depth beyond the norm accepted by the associated community."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep_diving"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deep diving","blocks":[{"text":"Deep diving is underwater diving to a depth beyond the normal range accepted by the associated community. In some cases this is a prescribed limit established by an authority, while in others it is associated with a level of certification or training, and it may vary depending on whether the diving is recreational, technical or commercial. Nitrogen narcosis becomes a hazard below 30 metres (98 ft) and hypoxic breathing gas is required below 60 metres (200 ft) to lessen the risk of oxygen toxicity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Trevor_Jackson_returns_from_SS_Kyogle.jpg/330px-Trevor_Jackson_returns_from_SS_Kyogle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_diving"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/500px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/500px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Technical divers preparing for a mixed-gas decompression dive. Note the backplate and wing setup with side mounted stage tanks containing EAN50 (left side) and pure oxygen (right side).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADecompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Plongee-RecycleurInspiration_20040221-153656.jpg/500px-Plongee-RecycleurInspira